 balls. Let ball have label 1 if it is blue, 0 otherwise."],"metadata":{"id":"oYZbfCrZt9i7"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["balls = [1 for i in range(9)] + [0 for i in range(11)]"],"metadata":{"id":"f4qxHHTGudSa"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# two groups\n","balls_left = [1 for i in range(8)] + [0 for i in range(5)]  # 8 blue and 5 yellow\n","balls_right = [1 for i in range(1)] + [0 for i in range(6)]  # 1 blue and 6 yellow"],"metadata":{"id":"KPFIH6sJvzC6"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Implement a function to calculate the Shannon Entropy"],"metadata":{"id":"0or9V2GdmAVw"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def entropy(a_list):\n","    values, counts = np.unique(a_list, return_counts=True)\n","\n","    total = len(a_list)\n","    entropy = 0\n","\n","    for count in counts:\n","        p = count / total\n","        entropy -= p * np.log2(p)\n","\n","    return entropy\n","    pass"],"metadata":{"id":"u3AH-IZ4xDlj"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Tests"],"metadata":{"id":"gRSRkrfHxY2y"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["print(entropy(balls))  # 9 blue и 11 yellow\n","print(entropy(balls_left))  # 8 blue и 5 yellow\n","print(entropy(balls_right))  # 1 blue и 6 yellow\n","print(entropy([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]))  # entropy of a fair 6-sided die"],"metadata":{"id":"c1mkoWimxZ0Z","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790693239907,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":14,"user":{"displayName":"Gabriel Lima","userId":"02315840675971190662"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"ae555d23-ed9f-484b-e489-65644eaf07b4"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["0.9927744539878083\n","0.9612366047228759\n","0.5916727785823275\n","2.584962500721156\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["3. What is the entropy of the state given by the list balls_left?"],"metadata":{"id":"QpqzWECLo9O5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["0.961"],"metadata":{"id":"SpqAiJ6BpJzJ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["4. What is the entropy of a fair die? (where we look at a die as a system with 6 equally probable states)?"],"metadata":{"id":"JnmXBWBWpSqp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["2.585"],"metadata":{"id":"HYqUyBf5pUXA"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# information gain calculation\n","def information_gain(root, left, right):\n","    \"\"\" root - initial data, left and right - two partitions of initial data\"\"\"\n","    return entropy(root) - (len(left) / len(root)) * entropy(left) - (len(right) / len(root)) * entropy(right)"],"metadata":{"id":"pfJEOi9FpXIg"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["5. What is the information gain from splitting the initial dataset into balls_left and balls_right ?"],"metadata":{"id":"IOmDu64dpoaB"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["print(information_gain(balls, balls_left, balls_right))"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"6oJAalAgpq4o","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790693573139,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":6,"user":{"displayName":"Gabriel Lima","userId":"02315840675971190662"}},"outputId":"a1eeba49-5eae-40c0-a826-5cef0fc35801"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["0.16088518841412436\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def information_gains(X, y):\n","    \"\"\"Outputs information gain when splitting with each feature\"\"\"\n","    out = []\n","    for i in X.columns:\n","        out.append(information_gain(y, y[X[i] == 0], y[X[i] == 1]))\n","    return out"],"metadata":{"id":"Z_HHUDe6p5vw"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}